2026-10-07T14:33:23.2972908Z [36;1m# --bazel-flag=--config=ruff reuses the same aspect + toolchain configuration as[0m
2026-10-07T14:33:23.2973257Z [36;1m# `bazel test --config=ruff` (see quality/static_analysis/static_analysis.bazelrc) —[0m
2026-10-07T14:33:23.2973630Z [36;1m# the aspect is deliberately NOT also passed via `--aspect=` here, since Bazel rejects the same aspect[0m
2026-10-07T14:33:23.2973916Z [36;1m# being registered twice.[0m
2026-10-07T14:33:23.2974086Z [36;1m#[0m
2026-10-07T14:33:23.2974343Z [36;1m# --bazel-flag=--build_event_json_file writes a Build Event Protocol JSON stream alongside the build, letting[0m
2026-10-07T14:33:23.2974767Z [36;1m# us enumerate every emitted rules_lint_machine SARIF report file below without crawling bazel-bin with[0m
2026-10-07T14:33:23.2975045Z [36;1m# `find`.[0m
2026-10-07T14:33:23.2975167Z [36;1m#[0m
2026-10-07T14:33:23.2975434Z [36;1m# The three github-*:enabled=false flags disable Aspect CLI features that post PR comments / check runs /[0m
2026-10-07T14:33:23.2975859Z [36;1m# status comments directly via Aspect's own hosted backend (requires `aspect auth login` / an Aspect-managed[0m
2026-10-07T14:33:23.2976717Z [36;1m# GitHub App). We deliberately don't use those — findings are surfaced via the SARIF upload below instead,[0m
2026-10-07T14:33:23.2977032Z [36;1m# using only the standard GITHUB_TOKEN.[0m
2026-10-07T14:33:23.2977200Z [36;1m#[0m
2026-10-07T14:33:23.2977454Z [36;1m# --artifact-upload:enabled=false disables the CLI's own attempt to upload its internal Build Event artifact[0m
2026-10-07T14:33:23.2977886Z [36;1m# via GitHub's native ArtifactService (this uses GitHub's own OIDC token, not Aspect's backend, but would need[0m
2026-10-07T14:33:23.2978296Z [36;1m# `id-token: write` and isn't needed here since we collect/upload the SARIF report ourselves below).[0m
2026-10-07T14:33:23.2978564Z [36;1m#[0m
2026-10-07T14:33:23.2978814Z [36;1m# Ideally, merge gating for newly introduced findings would be handled by a branch ruleset that blocks PRs[0m
2026-10-07T14:33:23.2979236Z [36;1m# with Code Scanning alerts above a configured severity, using GitHub's own new-vs-baseline diff instead of[0m
2026-10-07T14:33:23.2979653Z [36;1m# Aspect's locally computed one. That's blocked for now on otterdog support for the `code_scanning` ruleset[0m
2026-10-07T14:33:23.2980059Z [36;1m# rule (see eclipse-csi/otterdog#639). Until that lands, fall back to gating via aspect's own exit code:[0m
2026-10-07T14:33:23.2980654Z [36;1m# `--strategy=hold-the-line` (fails only on error-severity diagnostics) for PR/push/merge_group runs, where[0m
2026-10-07T14:33:23.2981196Z [36;1m# the result should actually gate the job;[0m
2026-10-07T14:33:23.2981684Z [36;1m# `--strategy=soft` (never fails) for other triggers (e.g. nightly, manual dispatch), which only want the[0m
2026-10-07T14:33:23.2981996Z [36;1m# report/SARIF, not a pass/fail verdict.[0m
2026-10-07T14:33:23.2982182Z [36;1mcase "pull_request" in[0m
2026-10-07T14:33:23.2982385Z [36;1m  pull_request|push|merge_group) STRATEGY=hold-the-line ;;[0m
2026-10-07T14:33:23.2982598Z [36;1m  *) STRATEGY=soft ;;[0m
